pocket-motion-only: a filter layer renders a span of the draw list offscreen, reads it back, blurs it and composites it by reading the destination; the PSP GE, ESP32 PPA, Symbian GLES2 and Vita GXM backends draw ops into a framebuffer they never read back, and have neither the second target nor the arithmetic. No upstream backend is taught LAYER_PUSH or LAYER_POP; a stream carrying them stops there.

0018 — filter layers: a node and its whole subtree painted into one
transparent layer that is blurred (`blur-*`), given a drop shadow or glow
(`drop-shadow-*`, `text-shadow-*`, `glow-*`) and composited by blend mode
(`mix-blend-*`). Blur deviation and every shadow parameter are
keyframe-animatable, including as a CSS `filter` value.

What the patch adds, by file:

- `contracts/spec/spec.ts`, `gen-rust.ts`, `engine/core/src/spec.rs`
  (regenerated): props `blur` (163), `dropShadowX/Y/Blur/Color/Gain`
  (164-168), `blendMode` (169); the first six animatable (bits 41-46,
  timeline-only); enum `BlendMode` {Normal, Multiply, Screen, Overlay,
  Add}; `DRAW_OP.layerPush = 67`, `layerPop = 68`; `LAYER_MAX_DEPTH = 4`;
  `BLUR_MAX = 128`.
- `framework/compiler/tailwind.ts`: `blur`, `blur-sm..3xl`, `blur-none`,
  `blur-[Npx]`; `drop-shadow-[X_Y(_B)(_#hex)]`, `drop-shadow-<color>`,
  `drop-shadow-none` and the same under `text-shadow-`; `glow-[B]`,
  `glow-<color>`, `glow-gain-[N]`; `mix-blend-normal|multiply|screen|
  overlay|plus-lighter|add`.
- `framework/compiler/animation.ts`: keyframe properties `blur`,
  `dropShadowX/Y/Blur/Color/Gain`, and `filter` with `blur()` and
  `drop-shadow()` functions.
- `engine/core/src/style.rs`: the seven fields; gain defaults to 1.
- `engine/core/src/draw.rs`: `paint` brackets a node that has a filter
  in LAYER_PUSH/LAYER_POP around `paint_body` — the rest of the old
  `paint`, moved unchanged — so every early return is inside the layer.
  Past LAYER_MAX_DEPTH the node paints unfiltered. A node with no filter
  prop emits exactly the words it did before.
- `engine/core/src/raster.rs`: `render_ops` renders the span into a
  pooled full-frame `LayerTarget` (RgbaTarget's own arithmetic, touched
  rows tracked) and `composite_layer` filters it: the blur is three
  extended-box passes per axis (Gwosdek et al. 2011, so the picture moves
  continuously with the deviation), integer, at 1/2, 1/4 or 1/8 resolution
  above 8, 16 and 32 px deviation; the shadow is the layer's alpha offset
  by whole physical px, blurred the same way, times gain, tinted; the
  layer goes over its shadow and the result over the target by W3C
  separable blending then source-over. A target that cannot read its
  backdrop blends as normal. `RenderTarget::read` is the new trait method.
- `engine/core/src/damage.rs`: the two word counts; a change inside a
  layer, or to its parameters, is a full redraw, because a filter spreads
  a change past the op that made it.
- `engine/core/src/tests.rs`: nine tests — no layer without a filter prop,
  blur symmetric and continuous in its deviation, the step at each
  resolution change bounded (measured 1 level), shadow offset and gain,
  the four blend functions exactly, the depth limit keeping the stream
  going, a change inside a layer redrawn in full and equal to the full
  render, glow around a stroked run, and a pooled buffer carrying nothing
  from the layer before (red with the clear removed).

